  "result": "I fixed it. When an option had both a short and a long name, the help output listed them backwards: `@click.option(\"-v\", \"--verbose\")` showed up as `--verbose, -v` instead of the usual `-v, --verbose`.\n\n**Cause:** `join_options` in `src/click/formatting.py:319` builds the names column by sorting each option's names by prefix length. It sorted with `reverse=True`, which put the longest prefix (`--`) first. I removed `reverse=True`, so short names now come first, as they do in upstream Click:\n\n```\nOptions:\n  --version      Show the version and exit.\n  --zeta TEXT    Z\n  --alpha TEXT   A\n  -v, --verbose  V\n  --help         Show this message and exit.\n```\n\nThe whole test suite passes (1906 passed, 102 skipped). I didn't add a regression test for this.\n\nI also checked the order of the options themselves. They appear in the order you declare them in code. That's normal Click behaviour, not part of this bug, so I left it alone. If you meant something like sorting options alphabetically, tell me and I'll change that too.\n\nI haven't committed the change.",
